# Rail-optimized 1024-GPU compute fabric (DGX SuperPOD-class), 2-tier leaf-spine.
#
#   1024 GPUs = 128 servers x 8 GPUs; each GPU has its own 200G NIC -> its own rail.
#   8 rails; rail r is served by 4 leaf switches, each covering 32 servers
#   (32 downlinks = GPU r of servers 32j..32j+31) + 32 uplinks  => 64-port leaf.
#   32 leaves total (8 rails x 4), 32 spines of radix 32, NON-BLOCKING.
#
#   "Rails 8" switches the host->leaf attachment from consecutive to rail-strided:
#       GPU g -> rail (g%8), server (g/8), leaf = rail*4 + (g/8)/32
#   so a leaf holds one GPU from each of 32 servers (a real rail), NOT 4 whole
#   servers. Everything else (routing, route construction) follows automatically.
#
#   NOTE: NVLink is NOT modelled. Intra-server traffic (same server, different
#   rail) therefore takes the rail->spine->rail path, i.e. the most expensive one,
#   which is inverted vs reality. Negligible for scattered patterns (~0.7% of a2a
#   flows) but pessimistic for ring collectives. See notes/.
Nodes 1024
Tiers 2
Podsize 1024
Rails 8

Tier 0
Oversubscribed 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 32
Radix_Up 32
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 32
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Bundle 1
